<title>BELGIUM: EU to meet on Wednesday to discuss swine fever.</title>
<headline>EU to meet on Wednesday to discuss swine fever.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's Standing Veterinary Committee will hold a special meeting on Wednesday to discuss swine fever, a Commission official said.</p>
<p>On Friday, the Dutch Agriculture Ministry said it had detected two new cases of swine fever, taking the number of affected farms to four, and confirmed that Poland had banned the import of pigs from the Netherlands.</p>
<p>Germany earlier this week banned the export of pigs for slaughter from four German states after an outbreak of swine fever.</p>
<p>Belgium and Switzerland have announced curbs on imports of live pigs and pork meat from Germany.</p>
</text>
